  "notes": "MIMETIC TYPE:\nOnomatopoeia expressing hesitation and confusion.\n\nGRAMMATICAL FORMS:\n- まごまごする - to be at a loss (suru-verb)\n- まごまご（と）している - to be bewildered (state)\n\nUSAGE:\nImplies being flustered and unable to act decisively. Often used when someone is caught off guard or doesn't know how to respond to a situation.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- おろおろする - to be flustered (more panic)\n- うろうろする - to wander aimlessly (more physical)\n- もたもたする - to dawdle (more about slowness)\n- きょろきょろする - to look around restlessly",
